 "traps": [
  "package.json has no name (only private: true): the unit is named by its root and its dependencies have unit null",
  "the lockfile is pnpm-lock.yaml (lockfileVersion 6.0) while every script in package.json calls npm run and npx; no packageManager, engines, .nvmrc or CI file declares a version of Node or of pnpm, so toolchains is empty, and the lockfile format is not a pnpm version",
  "resolved is the version in the importer block of pnpm-lock.yaml without the peer suffix: next is 14.2.3, not 14.2.3(react-dom@18.3.1)(react@18.3.1); the packages: section holds the transitive ones",
  "eslint-config-next is pinned at 14.1.0 while next is 14.2.3; @stripe/stripe-js, lucide-react, next and eslint-config-next are exact pins, the others are caret ranges",
  "tailwindcss, tailwind-merge and tailwindcss-animate are in dependencies, not devDependencies; supabase in devDependencies is the Supabase CLI, not the client (@supabase/supabase-js and @supabase/ssr)",
  "the stripe command of the stripe:* scripts is the Stripe CLI, installed by no manifest; stripe in dependencies is the server SDK and @stripe/stripe-js the browser one",
  "types_db.ts is generated by supabase gen types (script supabase:generate-types) and is committed in UTF-16 little-endian with a byte order mark and CRLF: a reader that assumes UTF-8 sees binary or another language; .prettierignore skips it",
  "next-env.d.ts says it should not be edited; tsconfig.json also includes .next/types/**/*.ts, which exist only after next dev or next build",
  "there is no next.config file and no ESLint configuration although next lint and five ESLint packages are declared",
  "tsconfig.json sets baseUrl . with @/* to ./*, the repository root (there is no src directory); some imports use the bare baseUrl form instead of the alias: types_db in utils/supabase/admin.ts, styles/main.css in app/layout.tsx",
  "one unit holds browser and server code: 'use client' components, 'use server' actions (utils/auth-helpers/server.ts, utils/stripe/server.ts), three route handlers found by file convention and middleware.ts at the root, outside app/",
  "schema.sql and supabase/migrations/20230530034630_init.sql are the same 144 lines, hand-written; both define a plpgsql trigger function, so Linguist calls them PLpgSQL and not SQL; supabase/seed.sql is empty",
  "Supabase and Stripe are hosted services seen only through their SDKs and environment variables (.env.local.example); supabase/config.toml describes the local Supabase stack: Postgres 15, the Inbucket mail catcher, GitHub as the one enabled OAuth provider, Twilio disabled",
  "utils/supabase/admin.ts uses the service role key and writes the tables that the Stripe webhook (app/api/webhooks/route.ts) keeps in sync; the row level security policies live in schema.sql",
  "Vercel shows only as the NEXT_PUBLIC_VERCEL_URL fallback in utils/helpers.ts: there is no vercel.json",
  "public/favicon.ico is a PNG image under an .ico name; the .svg logos in public/ are text and are not excluded",
  "tailwind.config.js lists pages/**/*.{ts,tsx} in content but there is no pages directory; components.json is the shadcn/ui configuration and components/ui is project code, not vendored",
  "fixtures/stripe-fixtures.json is input for the Stripe CLI (products and prices to create), not test data read by the code"
 ],
